  "description": "The Nua Luna Rohloff is a versatile titanium flat-bar bike built for commuting and light touring. Designed as a true do-everything platform, it combines Nua’s handcrafted Grade 9 titanium frame with the proven durability and low-maintenance performance of the Rohloff internal gear hub. Clean, quiet, and practical, it’s made for riders who want one reliable bike for everyday use and longer mixed-terrain rides. The frame delivers the smooth, resilient ride quality titanium is known for while remaining responsive under load. Practical details include mounts for racks, mudguards, and bottles, internal cable routing, and sliding dropouts for precise belt tension and adaptable setups. Built around real-world versatility, the Luna transitions easily from daily commuting to weekend exploration. The Rohloff hub, paired with a Gates Carbon Belt Drive, provides a wide gear range with minimal maintenance and consistent shifting in all conditions. The frame supports both 650B wheels up to 57 mm for comfort and off-road capability, or 700C wheels up to 44 mm for faster urban riding. The front end can be configured with either the Nua Carbon Adventure fork for lightweight performance or the Nua Titanium Type A fork for a fully titanium build. Stable geometry and a tapered headtube ensure confident handling whether commuting, carrying loads, or riding long mixed-surface routes. Available as a frameset or complete build, the Nua Luna Rohloff is a durable, adaptable titanium bike designed for riders who value simplicity, reliability, and everyday versatility.",
